% Oxygen and oxygen equipment: LCD L33797 and its Policy Article A52514 (DME
% MACs), read with NCD 240.2 (Home Use of Oxygen). A policy program of the
% DMEPOS model: it includes dmepos.le and states when a claim for stationary
% oxygen equipment (E0424, E0439, E1390, E1391), portable equipment (E0431,
% E0433, E0434, E1392, K0738) or oxygen contents (E0441–E0444, E0447) is
% REASONABLE AND NECESSARY: the qualifying blood gas study (ordered and
% evaluated by the treating practitioner, at the time of need, by a qualified
% provider — never the supplier), the hypoxemia of Groups I and II, the
% normoxemic Group III, the Group IV conditions that deny coverage, the
% portable system for a beneficiary mobile in the home who did not qualify
% during sleep only, and the continued coverage after the third month
% (Group II and III: a repeat qualifying study between the 61st and 90th day
% and a new order). The payment condition it adds: the 36-month rental cap on
% equipment (Policy Article A52514).
%
% How the criteria are read. Measurements are facts of the record: the
% arterial PO2 in mm Hg and the oxygen saturation in percent, taken at
% rest, during sleep or during exercise ("the arterial PO2 of B taken at
% rest is 54 mm Hg"); a fall below baseline during sleep; who performed the
% study and when. "At rest" is the awake, resting measurement the LCD calls
% "at rest (awake)" and "while awake". The Group II conditions and the Group
% IV conditions are documented conditions ("the medical record of B
% documents cor pulmonale"), from the lists below, as are the Group III
% conditions the literature shows oxygen improves (cluster headaches). One
% finding is a judgment: "oxygen will improve the condition" (initial
% coverage, all groups).
% Therapy is taken to start on the day the equipment is delivered. Not
% modelled: the flow rate above 4 LPM (a payment rate), the concurrent
% PAP-and-oxygen titration rules, the overnight-oximetry procedure (a home
% overnight oximetry counts as a study by an IDTF when the record says so).

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    % the record
    the arterial PO2 of *a beneficiary* taken *a condition* is *a number* mm Hg; undefined.
    the oxygen saturation of *a beneficiary* taken *a condition* is *a number* percent; undefined.
    the arterial PO2 of *a beneficiary* fell *a number* mm Hg below baseline during sleep; undefined.
    the oxygen saturation of *a beneficiary* fell *a number* percent below baseline during sleep; undefined.
    the blood gas study of *a beneficiary* was performed by *a performer*; undefined.
    the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of *a beneficiary*; undefined.
    the blood gas study of *a beneficiary* was performed at the time of need; undefined.
    the three exercise oximetry tests of *a beneficiary* were performed in one session; undefined.
    *a beneficiary* is mobile within the home; undefined.
    the repeat blood gas study of *a beneficiary* was performed on *a date*; undefined.
    the repeat arterial PO2 of *a beneficiary* is *a number* mm Hg; undefined.
    the repeat oxygen saturation of *a beneficiary* is *a number* percent; undefined.
    a new order for *an item* is dated *a date*; undefined.
    % derived
    *an item* is stationary oxygen equipment.
    *an item* is portable oxygen equipment.
    *an item* is oxygen contents.
    *a beneficiary* qualifies for home oxygen.
    *a performer* is a qualified performer of blood gas studies.
    the group of *a beneficiary* is *a group*.
    *a beneficiary* meets the Group I criteria.
    *a beneficiary* meets the Group II criteria.
    *a beneficiary* meets the Group III criteria.
    *a beneficiary* has a Group IV condition.
    *a condition* is a Group II condition.
    *a condition* is a Group IV condition.
    *a condition* is a symptom of hypoxemia.
    *a condition* is improved by oxygen per literature.
    *a beneficiary* is hypoxemic *a condition*.
    *a beneficiary* is normoxemic at rest.
    *a beneficiary* is borderline hypoxemic at rest.
    *a beneficiary* qualifies while awake.
    oxygen therapy with *an item* was initiated on *a date*.
    the continued coverage requirements for oxygen are met for *a claim*.
    the repeat blood gas study of *a beneficiary* is qualifying for *a group*.

the knowledge base oxygen includes these resources:
    dmepos.

the knowledge base oxygen includes:

LCD L33797 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/lcd.aspx?lcdid=33797".
the text of LCD L33797 is at "sources/lcd/L33797.txt".
Policy Article A52514 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/article.aspx?articleid=52514".
the text of Policy Article A52514 is at "sources/article/A52514.txt".
NCD 240 2 is published at "https://www.cms.gov/medicare-coverage-database/view/ncd.aspx?ncdid=169".
the text of NCD 240 2 is at "sources/ncd/NCD_240.2.txt".

% What the equipment is, by code (Policy Article A52514).
rule oxygen_stationary_codes with provenance Policy Article A52514,
        confer "Payment for oxygen contents (stationary and/or portable) is included in the allowance for stationary equipment (E0424, E0439, E1390, E1391)":
an item is stationary oxygen equipment
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0424", "E0439", "E1390", "E1391"].

rule oxygen_portable_codes with provenance Policy Article A52514,
        confer "If use of portable equipment (E0431, E0433, E0434, E1392, K0738) begins after the use of stationary equipment begins":
an item is portable oxygen equipment
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0431", "E0433", "E0434", "E1392", "K0738"].

rule oxygen_contents_codes with provenance Policy Article A52514,
        confer "payment for both stationary contents (E0441 or E0442) and portable contents (E0443, E0444 or E0447) begins when the rental for the stationary equipment ends":
an item is oxygen contents
    if the HCPCS code of the item is a code
    and the code is in ["E0441", "E0442", "E0443", "E0444", "E0447"].

% therapy starts with the delivery of the equipment: a device of this model
rule oxygen_initiation:
oxygen therapy with an item was initiated on a date
    if the item was delivered on the date.

section applicability is:

rule oxygen_codes with provenance Policy Article A52514,
        confer "Oxygen and oxygen equipment is covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the policy for code a code is oxygen
    if the code is in ["E0424", "E0439", "E1390", "E1391", "E0431", "E0433", "E0434", "E1392", "K0738", "E0441", "E0442", "E0443", "E0444", "E0447"].

rule oxygen_benefit with provenance Policy Article A52514,
        confer "Oxygen and oxygen equipment is covered under the Durable Medical Equipment benefit":
the benefit category of code a code is durable medical equipment
    if the policy for code the code is oxygen.

section question is:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The claims: stationary equipment, portable equipment, contents.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule oxygen_stationary with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "Home oxygen and oxygen equipment is covered only when both the":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is stationary oxygen equipment
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary qualifies for home oxygen
    and the continued coverage requirements for oxygen are met for the claim.

rule oxygen_portable with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "A portable oxygen system is covered if the beneficiary is mobile within the home for Groups I and II, and the qualifying blood gas study was performed while at rest (awake) or during exercise":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is portable oxygen equipment
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary qualifies for home oxygen
    and the beneficiary is mobile within the home
    and the beneficiary qualifies while awake
    and the continued coverage requirements for oxygen are met for the claim.

rule oxygen_contents with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "Oxygen contents are reimbursed with a monthly allowance covering all contents necessary for the month":
a claim is reasonable and necessary
    if the claim is for an item
    and the item is oxygen contents
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the beneficiary qualifies for home oxygen
    and the continued coverage requirements for oxygen are met for the claim.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Initial coverage: the qualifying study, the group, no Group IV condition.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule oxygen_qualifies with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "Initial coverage of home oxygen therapy and oxygen equipment is reasonable and necessary for Groups I and II if all of the following conditions are met":
a beneficiary qualifies for home oxygen
    if the treating practitioner ordered and evaluated the blood gas study of the beneficiary
    and the blood gas study of the beneficiary was performed at the time of need
    and the blood gas study of the beneficiary was performed by a performer
    and the performer is a qualified performer of blood gas studies
    and the group of the beneficiary is a group
    and the finding oxygen will improve the condition about the beneficiary is established
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary has a Group IV condition.

% Who may perform the study: not the supplier.
treating practitioner is a qualified performer of blood gas studies,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "the test be performed by a provider who is qualified to bill Medicare for the test – i.e., a Part A provider, a laboratory, an Independent Diagnostic Testing Facility (IDTF), or a treating practitioner".
laboratory is a qualified performer of blood gas studies,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "the test be performed by a provider who is qualified to bill Medicare for the test – i.e., a Part A provider, a laboratory, an Independent Diagnostic Testing Facility (IDTF), or a treating practitioner".
independent diagnostic testing facility is a qualified performer of blood gas studies,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "the test be performed by a provider who is qualified to bill Medicare for the test – i.e., a Part A provider, a laboratory, an Independent Diagnostic Testing Facility (IDTF), or a treating practitioner".
hospital is a qualified performer of blood gas studies,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "These prohibitions do not extend to blood gas studies performed by a hospital certified to do such tests".
% "A supplier is not considered a qualified provider or a qualified
% laboratory for purposes of this policy": no fact for the DME supplier.

rule oxygen_group_1 with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "Group I criteria include any of the following":
the group of a beneficiary is group 1
    if the beneficiary meets the Group I criteria.

rule oxygen_group_2 with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "Group II criteria include all of the following":
the group of a beneficiary is group 2
    if the beneficiary meets the Group II criteria.

rule oxygen_group_3 with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "Initial coverage of home oxygen therapy and oxygen equipment is reasonable and necessary for beneficiaries in Group III, if all of the following conditions are met":
the group of a beneficiary is group 3
    if the beneficiary meets the Group III criteria.

% Hypoxemia: a PO2 at or below 55 mm Hg or a saturation at or below 88
% percent, under the condition of the test (at rest, during sleep, during
% exercise); normoxemia at rest: a PO2 at or above 56 or a saturation at or
% above 89.
rule oxygen_hypoxemic_po2 with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "An arterial PO 2 at or below 55 mm Hg or an arterial oxygen saturation at or below 88 percent taken at rest (awake) while breathing room air":
a beneficiary is hypoxemic a condition
    if the arterial PO2 of the beneficiary taken the condition is a number mm Hg
    and the number <= 55.

rule oxygen_hypoxemic_saturation with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "An arterial PO 2 at or below 55 mm Hg or an arterial oxygen saturation at or below 88 percent taken at rest (awake) while breathing room air":
a beneficiary is hypoxemic a condition
    if the oxygen saturation of the beneficiary taken the condition is a number percent
    and the number <= 88.

rule oxygen_normoxemic_po2 with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "for a beneficiary who demonstrates an arterial PO2 at or above 56 mm Hg or an arterial oxygen saturation at or above 89 percent while awake":
a beneficiary is normoxemic at rest
    if the arterial PO2 of the beneficiary taken at rest is a number mm Hg
    and the number >= 56.

rule oxygen_normoxemic_saturation with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "for a beneficiary who demonstrates an arterial PO2 at or above 56 mm Hg or an arterial oxygen saturation at or above 89 percent while awake":
a beneficiary is normoxemic at rest
    if the oxygen saturation of the beneficiary taken at rest is a number percent
    and the number >= 89.

% Group I, criterion 1: hypoxemic at rest.
rule oxygen_group_1_rest with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "An arterial PO 2 at or below 55 mm Hg or an arterial oxygen saturation at or below 88 percent taken at rest (awake) while breathing room air":
a beneficiary meets the Group I criteria
    if the beneficiary is hypoxemic at rest.

% Group I, criterion 2: hypoxemic during sleep, normoxemic awake.
rule oxygen_group_1_sleep with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "taken during sleep for a beneficiary who demonstrates an arterial PO2 at or above 56 mm Hg or an arterial oxygen saturation at or above 89 percent while awake":
a beneficiary meets the Group I criteria
    if the beneficiary is hypoxemic during sleep
    and the beneficiary is normoxemic at rest.

% Group I, criterion 3: a fall during sleep with symptoms of hypoxemia.
rule oxygen_group_1_fall_po2 with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "A decrease in arterial PO 2 more than 10 mm Hg, or a decrease in arterial oxygen saturation more than 5 percent from baseline saturation, taken during sleep and associated with symptoms of hypoxemia":
a beneficiary meets the Group I criteria
    if the arterial PO2 of the beneficiary fell a number mm Hg below baseline during sleep
    and the number > 10
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a symptom of hypoxemia.

rule oxygen_group_1_fall_saturation with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "A decrease in arterial PO 2 more than 10 mm Hg, or a decrease in arterial oxygen saturation more than 5 percent from baseline saturation, taken during sleep and associated with symptoms of hypoxemia":
a beneficiary meets the Group I criteria
    if the oxygen saturation of the beneficiary fell a number percent below baseline during sleep
    and the number > 5
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a symptom of hypoxemia.

impairment of cognitive processes is a symptom of hypoxemia,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "symptoms of hypoxemia such as impairment of cognitive processes and nocturnal restlessness or insomnia".
nocturnal restlessness is a symptom of hypoxemia,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "symptoms of hypoxemia such as impairment of cognitive processes and nocturnal restlessness or insomnia".
insomnia is a symptom of hypoxemia,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "symptoms of hypoxemia such as impairment of cognitive processes and nocturnal restlessness or insomnia".

% Group I, criterion 4: hypoxemic during exercise, normoxemic at rest, the
% three tests of one session.
rule oxygen_group_1_exercise with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "taken during exercise for a beneficiary who demonstrates an arterial PO 2 at or above 56 mm Hg or an arterial oxygen saturation at or above 89 percent during the day while at rest":
a beneficiary meets the Group I criteria
    if the beneficiary is hypoxemic during exercise
    and the beneficiary is normoxemic at rest
    and the three exercise oximetry tests of the beneficiary were performed in one session.

% Group II: a PO2 of 56–59 or a saturation of 89 at rest, with a listed
% condition.
rule oxygen_borderline_po2 with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "An arterial PO 2 of 56-59 mm Hg or an arterial blood oxygen saturation of 89 percent":
a beneficiary is borderline hypoxemic at rest
    if the arterial PO2 of the beneficiary taken at rest is a number mm Hg
    and the number >= 56
    and the number <= 59.

rule oxygen_borderline_saturation with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "An arterial PO 2 of 56-59 mm Hg or an arterial blood oxygen saturation of 89 percent":
a beneficiary is borderline hypoxemic at rest
    if the oxygen saturation of the beneficiary taken at rest is a number percent
    and the number = 89.

rule oxygen_group_2_criteria with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "Group II criteria include all of the following":
a beneficiary meets the Group II criteria
    if the beneficiary is borderline hypoxemic at rest
    and the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a Group II condition.

dependent edema suggesting congestive heart failure is a Group II condition,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "Dependent edema suggesting congestive heart failure".
pulmonary hypertension is a Group II condition,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "Pulmonary hypertension or cor pulmonale, determined by measurement of pulmonary artery pressure, gated blood pool scan, echocardiogram".
cor pulmonale is a Group II condition,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "Pulmonary hypertension or cor pulmonale, determined by measurement of pulmonary artery pressure, gated blood pool scan, echocardiogram".
erythrocythemia with a hematocrit greater than 56 percent is a Group II condition,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "Erythrocythemia with a hematocrit greater than 56 percent".

% Group III: no hypoxemia of Groups I and II, and a condition the literature
% shows oxygen improves (a finding).
rule oxygen_group_3_criteria with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "A medical condition with distinct physiologic, cognitive, and/or functional symptoms documented in high-quality, peer-reviewed literature to be improved by oxygen therapy, such as cluster headaches":
a beneficiary meets the Group III criteria
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is improved by oxygen per literature
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary meets the Group I criteria
    and it is not the case that
        the beneficiary meets the Group II criteria.

% the conditions the literature shows oxygen improves: the LCD names cluster
% headaches ("not all inclusive"); another is added here with its evidence
cluster headaches is improved by oxygen per literature,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "documented in high-quality, peer-reviewed literature to be improved by oxygen therapy, such as cluster headaches".

% Group IV: conditions that deny coverage.
rule oxygen_group_4 with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "Oxygen therapy and oxygen equipment will also be denied as not reasonable and necessary if any of the following conditions are present":
a beneficiary has a Group IV condition
    if the medical record of the beneficiary documents a condition
    and the condition is a Group IV condition.

angina pectoris without hypoxemia is a Group IV condition,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "Angina pectoris in the absence of hypoxemia".
dyspnea without cor pulmonale or hypoxemia is a Group IV condition,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "Dyspnea without cor pulmonale or evidence of hypoxemia".
peripheral vascular disease with desaturation of an extremity only is a Group IV condition,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "Severe peripheral vascular disease resulting in clinically evident desaturation in one or more extremities but in the absence of systemic hypoxemia".
terminal illness not affecting breathing is a Group IV condition,
    as stated in LCD L33797, confer "Terminal illnesses that do not affect the ability to breathe".

% A portable system needs a qualification while awake: at rest, during
% exercise, or Group II (a resting measurement) — not during sleep only.
rule oxygen_awake_rest with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "If the only qualifying blood gas study was performed during sleep, portable oxygen will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a beneficiary qualifies while awake
    if the beneficiary is hypoxemic at rest.

rule oxygen_awake_exercise with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "If the only qualifying blood gas study was performed during sleep, portable oxygen will be denied as not reasonable and necessary":
a beneficiary qualifies while awake
    if the beneficiary is hypoxemic during exercise
    and the beneficiary is normoxemic at rest
    and the three exercise oximetry tests of the beneficiary were performed in one session.

rule oxygen_awake_group_2 with provenance LCD L33797,
        confer "A portable oxygen system is covered if the beneficiary is mobile within the home for Groups I and II, and the qualifying blood gas study was performed while at rest (awake) or during exercise":
a beneficiary qualifies while awake
    if the beneficiary meets the Group II criteria.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Continued coverage after the third month.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% the first three months need nothing beyond the initial qualification
rule oxygen_initial_months with provenance Policy Article A52514,
        confer "DOCUMENTATION FOR CONTINUED PAYMENT OF OXYGEN AFTER INITIAL COVERAGE":
the continued coverage requirements for oxygen are met for a claim
    if the rental month of the claim is a number
    and the number <= 3.

rule oxygen_continued_group_1 with provenance Policy Article A52514,
        confer "Group I While there is no formal requirement for re-evaluation and retesting":
the continued coverage requirements for oxygen are met for a claim
    if the rental month of the claim is a number
    and the number >= 4
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the group of the beneficiary is group 1.

rule oxygen_continued_group_2_3 with provenance Policy Article A52514,
        confer "Evaluation and documentation of a repeat qualifying blood gas test by the treating practitioner between the 61 st and 90 th days after initiation of therapy":
the continued coverage requirements for oxygen are met for a claim
    if the rental month of the claim is a number
    and the number >= 4
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is furnished to a beneficiary
    and the group of the beneficiary is a group
    and the group is in [group 2, group 3]
    and oxygen therapy with the item was initiated on a date
    and the repeat blood gas study of the beneficiary was performed on an other date
    and the other date is a second number days after the date
    and the second number >= 61
    and the second number <= 90
    and the repeat blood gas study of the beneficiary is qualifying for the group
    and a new order for the item is dated a third date
    and the third date is after the date.

% the repeat study qualifies for Group II when it shows the Group I or Group
% II values again; for Group III when it is normoxemic
rule oxygen_repeat_group_2_po2 with provenance Policy Article A52514,
        confer "Evaluation and documentation of a repeat qualifying blood gas test by the treating practitioner between the 61 st and 90 th days after initiation of therapy":
the repeat blood gas study of a beneficiary is qualifying for group 2
    if the repeat arterial PO2 of the beneficiary is a number mm Hg
    and the number <= 59.

rule oxygen_repeat_group_2_saturation with provenance Policy Article A52514,
        confer "Evaluation and documentation of a repeat qualifying blood gas test by the treating practitioner between the 61 st and 90 th days after initiation of therapy":
the repeat blood gas study of a beneficiary is qualifying for group 2
    if the repeat oxygen saturation of the beneficiary is a number percent
    and the number <= 89.

rule oxygen_repeat_group_3_po2 with provenance Policy Article A52514,
        confer "Evaluation and documentation of a repeat, normoxemic, qualifying blood gas test by the treating practitioner between the 61 st and 90 th days after initiation of therapy":
the repeat blood gas study of a beneficiary is qualifying for group 3
    if the repeat arterial PO2 of the beneficiary is a number mm Hg
    and the number >= 60.

rule oxygen_repeat_group_3_saturation with provenance Policy Article A52514,
        confer "Evaluation and documentation of a repeat, normoxemic, qualifying blood gas test by the treating practitioner between the 61 st and 90 th days after initiation of therapy":
the repeat blood gas study of a beneficiary is qualifying for group 3
    if the repeat oxygen saturation of the beneficiary is a number percent
    and the number >= 90.

section remedy is:

% The 36-month cap: no payment for equipment after the 36th rental month
% during the equipment's reasonable useful lifetime; contents are paid on.
rule oxygen_rental_cap with provenance Policy Article A52514,
        confer "There is no further payment for oxygen equipment during the 5-year reasonable useful lifetime (RUL) of the equipment after 36 rental payments have been made":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is oxygen
    and the claim is for an item
    and the rental month of the claim is a number
    and the number <= 36.

rule oxygen_contents_payment with provenance Policy Article A52514,
        confer "Contents are separately payable for beneficiary-owned gaseous or liquid systems":
the policy specific documentation requirements are met for a claim
    if the policy of the claim is oxygen
    and the claim is for an item
    and the item is oxygen contents.
